--- a/.agent/README.md
+++ b/.agent/README.md
@@ -6,6 +6,8 @@ Central index for Sygenti docs.
 
 - **App Feature Inventory (Apr 26, 2026)**: Map of features from docs, FE pages, BE tRPC routers, shared packages, tests. See [System/app_feature_inventory_apr_2026.md](./System/app_feature_inventory_apr_2026.md).
 
+- **Sygenti blind spot diagnostic (Aug 20, 2026)** — new public, unauthenticated `/diagnostic` marketing tool: fifteen questions on one named initiative → pillar bands (Organisation/Team/Self), up to three "mirror" contradictions, an archetype headline, three recommendations, one ask. Pure scoring/mirror/archetype logic lives in `@pulse/shared/diagnostic` (framework-agnostic, `bun:test`, 59 tests), computed client-side for an instant network-independent reveal and recomputed server-side as the stored system of record. New `marketing` Postgres schema, single `diagnostic_submissions` table upserted by session id (migration `0313`, hand-authored then tool-verified zero-drift against a real `drizzle-kit generate` once `bun install` unstalled). BE mirrors `ContactModule`'s public/rate-limited/no-RBAC pattern exactly (`DiagnosticModule`, oRPC branch `diagnostic`). `/diagnostic` had to be added to the AuthKit middleware's public-path allowlist or it 307s to `/`. See [Tasks/2026-08-20-sygenti-blind-spot-diagnostic.md](./Tasks/2026-08-20-sygenti-blind-spot-diagnostic.md).
+
 - **Global workflows: readiness + siblings (Aug 20, 2026)** — `readiness_score`, `pm_agent`, `signal_reasoning`, and `memory_consolidation` are code-owned global workflows (pause / inspect / redrive) on the same `PipelineRunner` ledger as Signals and Knowledge. Producers stay intake-only. See [Tasks/2026-08-20-global-workflows-readiness-siblings.md](./Tasks/2026-08-20-global-workflows-readiness-siblings.md) + [System/database_schema.md](./System/database_schema.md) (global pipeline section).
 
 - **Sygenti Slack-like channels, reply threads, files (Aug 20, 2026)** — Remaps Sygenti `/inbox` from the 18/19 Aug "thread-as-room" POC onto Slack vocabulary: **channel** = room (left rail, **New channel** CTA), **thread** = reply branch (`?thread=`, never a rail CTA). Private channels, invites, and the server `@Sygenti` mention gate work against migration `0314`. `SygentiService.createThread` is removed (channels are the only top-level room; `createReplyThread` is the sole thread-creation path) and `assertChannelAccess` drops its `write?: boolean` param. `sygentiThreadSchema` gained a required `replyCount: number` field — the FE reply affordance ("Reply in thread" / "View thread" / "N replies") reads it straight off the wire instead of computing it client-side. The channel message stream got a full Slack-anatomy redesign — `SygentiMessageRow` + `sygenti-message-grouping.ts` (5-minute/same-day/same-author grouping, sticky day dividers, hover-revealed reply toolbar, `AGENT` badge), delegated to from `AgenticMessage` via `SygentiChannelChromeContext` (defaults `null`, so every non-Sygenti chat surface is untouched); the rail's `#` glyph is now `aria-hidden`. Channel Files stays view-only. See [Tasks/2026-08-20-sygenti-slack-threads.md](./Tasks/2026-08-20-sygenti-slack-threads.md) + [System/sygenti_poc.md](./System/sygenti_poc.md).
